---
// "How it works": sticky heading and copy on the left, four numbered steps joined by a vertical line on the right.
---

<section class="bg-bg py-20 sm:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-14 px-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-brand-600 uppercase dark:text-brand-400">How it works</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-fg sm:text-5xl">From scattered to settled in a single week</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-md text-lg leading-8 text-pretty text-muted">You do not need a rollout plan or a consultant. Most teams run their first calm week within days of signing up.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-button bg-brand-600 px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-brand-600/25 transition-colors hover:bg-brand-700 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brand-500">
        <span>Start your first week</span>
        <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M5 12h14" />
          <path d="M13 6l6 6-6 6" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    <ol class="relative">
      <li class="relative flex gap-6 pb-12">
        <div class="absolute top-12 bottom-0 left-6 w-px -translate-x-1/2 bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="relative flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-600 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-brand-600/25">1</span>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Bring your work in</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted">Import from Trello, Asana, Linear or a spreadsheet in a couple of clicks. Halcyon tidies duplicates and keeps your history.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="relative flex gap-6 pb-12">
        <div class="absolute top-12 bottom-0 left-6 w-px -translate-x-1/2 bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="relative flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line bg-brand-50 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-950/40 dark:text-brand-300">2</span>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Set the week on Monday</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted">Pick up to three priorities each. Halcyon flags anyone who is overloaded before the week begins, not on Thursday night.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="relative flex gap-6 pb-12">
        <div class="absolute top-12 bottom-0 left-6 w-px -translate-x-1/2 bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <span class="relative flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line bg-brand-50 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-950/40 dark:text-brand-300">3</span>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Work in peace</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted">Progress updates itself as tasks move. Short async check-ins replace the stand-up, and Quiet Hours keep evenings quiet.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="relative flex gap-6">
        <span class="relative flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line bg-brand-50 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-950/40 dark:text-brand-300">4</span>
        <div class="pt-2">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Wrap up on Friday</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-muted">A one-page recap shows what shipped, what slipped and why. Send it to stakeholders as is, then close the laptop.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
